1	//! The `delete-bookmark` subcommand: delete one bookmark locally and
2	//! on `origin`, the disposal a cycle's bookmark gets at Land, in one
3	//! invocation rather than `jj bookmark delete` and a `jj git push`.
4	//!
5	//! - The remote goes first, then the local, so a push that fails
6	//!   leaves the local bookmark, and a rerun finishes the job: a side
7	//!   already gone is no error.
8	//! - `--skip local` deletes the remote only, `--skip remote` the local
9	//!   only.
10	//! - The commits stay: jj keeps a commit visible after its bookmark is
11	//!   gone, so a deletion is undone by recreating the bookmark at the
12	//!   commit it prints.
13	//! - `-s w` deletes in the work repo, `-s a` in the agent repo, `-s b`
14	//!   in both, and `-s p` in the repo `-R` names, as it is.
15	//! - A failure restores the repo from a `jj op` snapshot when the
16	//!   remote was untouched.
17	
